nvml_pluginCollect NVML metricsVCollects power and temperature metrics using the NVIDIA Management Library (NVML)
 API"ÂOptions:
  -i | --interval  Sampling interval in milliseconds (default: 100)
  -g | --gpu-devices  GPUs to be sampled. Available options are: all, cuda-visible, or a comma-separated
                      list of GPU IDs (e.g., 0,1,3) (default: cuda-visible)

The power usage is collected in Watts using the `nvmlDeviceGetFieldValues` API
function.
The GPU temperature is collected in degrees Celsius with the
`nvmlDeviceGetTemperature` API function.
(
ß
dcgm_pluginCollect DCGM metricsBCollects metrics exposed by the Data Center GPU Manager (DCGM) API"óOptions:
--help                                Show this help message.
--metrics arg (=s-gpu,s-cpu,s-nvswitch)
                                      Comma-separated list of DCGM field 
                                      names to sample.
                                      Partial name matching is supported 
                                      (e.g. 'cpu_utilization_t' matches 
                                      'cpu_utilization_total').
                                      To see the full mapping from DCGM field
                                      names to field IDs, run: dcgmi dmon 
                                      --list.
--gpu arg (=all)                      Select GPUs ("all", "cuda-visible", or 
                                      "dcgm:<ID>[-<ID>][,...]" e.g. 
                                      "dcgm:0,dcgm:2-4", default: "all").
--cpu arg (=all)                      Select CPUs ("all" or 
                                      "dcgm:<ID>[-<ID>][,...]" e.g. 
                                      "dcgm:0,dcgm:2-4", default: "all").
--nvswitch arg (=all)                 Select NVSwitches ("all" or 
                                      "dcgm:<ID>[-<ID>][,...]" e.g. 
                                      "dcgm:0,dcgm:2-4", default: "all").
--nic arg (=all)                      Select NICs ("all" or 
                                      "dcgm:<ID>[-<ID>][,...]" e.g. 
                                      "dcgm:0,dcgm:2-4", default: "all").
--sampling-period arg (=100)          Sampling period in milliseconds. 
                                      Minimum allowed value is 100ms.
--hostengine-addr arg (=localhost:5555)
                                      Address of the DCGM hostengine 
                                      (host:port) or UDS path.
                                      When not specified, the plugin connects
                                      to localhost:5555 and falls back to 
                                      embedded DCGM if that connection fails.
(
¦
network_pluginCollect network adapter metrics5Collects network adapter metrics from /sys/class/net/"¹Options:
  -i | --interval  Sampling interval in microseconds (default: 100000)
  -d | --device    Device name as regular expression
                   (default: all physical devices)
  -m | --metric    Metric name as regular expression (default: .*_bytes)

To specify multiple devices and metrics the respective options can be used
multiple times and as regular expression.
When using `-d all` or `--device=all` all adapters will be considered (not only
physical ones).
When using `-m all` or `--metric=all` all metrics will be considered (not only
metrics in bytes).
(
